00:04:42,857 --> 00:04:48,857
Zombieland: Double Tap is a horror, comedy film directed by Ruben Fleischer.

2
00:09:25,714 --> 00:09:31,714
Columbus, Tallahassee, Wichita, and Little Rock move to the American heartland as they face off against
evolved zombies, fellow survivors, and the growing pains of the snarky makeshift family.

3
00:14:08,571 --> 00:14:14,571
Tallahassee, played by Woody Harrelson.

4
00:18:51,428 --> 00:18:57,428
Columbus, played by Jesse Eisenberg.

5
00:23:34,285 --> 00:23:40,285
Wichita, played by Emma Stone.

6
00:28:17,142 --> 00:28:23,142
Little Rock, played by Abigail Breslin.

7
00:32:59,999 --> 00:33:05,999
Madison, played by Zoey Deutch.

8
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Berkeley, played by Avan Jogia.

9
00:42:25,714 --> 00:42:31,714
Zombieland: Double Tap is a 2019 American post-apocalyptic zombie comedy film directed by
Ruben Fleischer and written by Rhett Reese, Paul Wernick, and David Callaham.

10
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
The sequel to Zombieland (2009), it stars an ensemble cast including Woody Harrelson, Jesse Eisenberg, Abigail Breslin, Emma
Stone (all reprising their roles), Rosario Dawson, Zoey Deutch, Avan Jogia, Luke Wilson, and Thomas Middleditch.

11
00:51:51,428 --> 00:51:57,428
In the sequel, Tallahassee (Harrelson), Columbus (Eisenberg), and Wichita (Stone) face evolved zombies and encounter
other survivors as they travel from the White House to Graceland to search for Little Rock (Breslin).

12
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
A sequel to the original film began development in November 2009, with the
returns of Reese, Wernick, Fleischer and the main cast planned.

13
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
It soon faced several delays, and the writers instead wrote a Zombieland television pilot in 2013
featuring a new cast, which ultimately failed in being ordered for a series release.

14
01:05:59,999 --> 01:06:05,999
Development for the sequel film was revived in February 2016, the screenplay was
completed in March 2017, and the film was confirmed in July 2018.

15
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
The rest of the cast was rounded out under a year later, and principal photography began in
January 2019 and concluded that March, with filming primarily taking place in Atlanta.

16
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
Zombieland: Double Tap premiered in Los Angeles on October 10, 2019, was theatrically
released in the United States on October 18, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

17
01:20:08,571 --> 01:20:14,571
It received mostly positive reviews from critics, who found it to be a worthwhile successor to the
original and praised the cast performances (particularly those of Stone and Deutch).

18
01:24:51,428 --> 01:24:57,428
The film grossed $125 million worldwide, surpassing its predecessor.

19
01:29:34,285 --> 01:29:40,285
The film explores themes of marriage proposal, the
white house, gore, road trip, sequel.

20
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
